        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix: prevent ClickClack startup backlog replay",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where ClickClack-backed OpenClaw channels could treat old ClickClack messages as new live input after a gateway restart when the ClickClack event backlog spans more than one HTTP page.\n\nThe old startup path advanced the cursor through only the first `/api/realtime/events` page before opening the websocket. ClickClack's websocket endpoint is allowed to replay events after the cursor it receives, so older events beyond that first page could be delivered to the OpenClaw channel adapter as if they were fresh messages.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe ClickClack gateway now defaults to tail-from-now startup behavior: it drains every historical event page to advance to the true tail cursor without dispatching those old events, then opens the websocket from that tail. Explicit historical dispatch remains available with `backfillOnStart: true`.\n\nThe change also adds in-process idempotency for repeated event ids and repeated message ids, covering HTTP/websocket overlap and duplicate websocket delivery during reconnects.\n\n## User Impact\n\nOperators can restart an OpenClaw gateway connected to a ClickClack workspace without old channel messages re-arming agent turns. New ClickClack messages still arrive normally after the gateway subscribes at the tail.\n\nFor operators who intentionally want startup backlog dispatch, `channels.clickclack.backfillOnStart: true` preserves that behavior as an explicit opt-in.\n\n## Evidence\n\nReal behavior proof from the stock ClickClack validation service on `http://127.0.0.1:8100`:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"environment\": {\n    \"clickclackUrl\": \"http://127.0.0.1:8100\",\n    \"workspaceId\": \"wsp_01ktq4zg...mcya\",\n    \"channelId\": \"chn_01ktq4zg...jts6\",\n    \"realServer\": true,\n    \"transport\": \"HTTP /api/realtime/events plus WebSocket /api/realtime/ws\"\n  },\n  \"staleCursorTrace\": {\n    \"firstHttpPageSize\": 200,\n    \"cursorAfterSinglePage\": \"cur_01ktyhdc...xf6a\",\n    \"websocketReplayCountFromSinglePageCursor\": 501,\n    \"replayFirstCursor\": \"cur_01ktyhep...vtrq\",\n    \"replayLastCursor\": \"cur_01kx2sf2...gyq7\"\n  },\n  \"fixedTailDrainTrace\": {\n    \"httpPagesFetchedUntilEmpty\": 39,\n    \"drainedEventCount\": 7428,\n    \"tailCursor\": \"cur_01kwv3nr...zegk\",\n    \"websocketReplayCountFromTailCursor\": 0\n  },\n  \"liveControl\": {\n    \"postedHumanMessageBody\": \"tail-drain-proof-1783578986767\",\n    \"postedMessageId\": \"msg_01kx2sf2...y8qz\",\n    \"receivedLiveEventType\": \"message.created\",\n    \"receivedLiveEventCursor\": \"cur_01kx2sf2...gyq7\",\n    \"receivedLiveEventMessageId\": \"msg_01kx2sf2...y8qz\"\n  },\n  \"conclusion\": \"PASS: real ClickClack server replays historical events from a stale single-page cursor, but not from the fully drained tail cursor; live events still arrive after tail subscription.\"\n}\n```\n\nFocused validation:\n\n```text\npnpm test:extension clickclack\nTest Files  6 passed (6)\nTests       41 passed (41)\n\npnpm tsgo:extensions\nPASS\n\npnpm build\nPASS\n\nnode --import tsx scripts/generate-bundled-channel-config-metadata.ts --check\nPASS\n\ngit diff --check\nPASS\n```\n\n`pnpm check` currently fails on the npm shrinkwrap guard both on this branch and on clean `origin/main` at `a905eb42ac`, so it appears to be base-state:\n\n```text\nfailed:1   npm shrinkwrap guard\n.: npm-shrinkwrap.json is stale. Run `pnpm deps:shrinkwrap:generate`.\n```\n\n`codex review --base origin/main` could not run in this environment because the local Codex CLI is not logged in and received OpenAI API 401 responses. I ran a local review plus an independent cross-family HyperReview-style review before opening.\n\nAI-assisted. Authored by ragesaq; code by Chisel using `openai/gpt-5.5`.\n",
        "branch": "fix/clickclack-startup-tail-drain",
